summary.label:
The tapping test is a neuropsychologsecondscal test that examines motor functioning, specifically, motor speed and lateralized coordination (click on the screen as often as possible). Duration of test: 5, 10, 20, 30, 60, 90, 120 second.
* Result:
- Average value of 5 second intervals;
- Number of taps;
- Duration of touches;
- Coefficient of nervous system's force, characteristic of force of nervous system(CNSF, test duration - 30 s);
Statistics of results of group of athletes.
* This app can be used by athletes and teachers of specialized educational institutions in their scientific research.
